 "title": "Microbial Metabolism and Fermentation Processes",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the metabolism and fermentation processes of various microorganisms, particularly Scheffersomyces stipitis and related species. The organisms, such as S. stipitis, R. toruloides, and L. starkeyi, consume glucose and xylose, producing ethanol, folate, and biomass. The pentose phosphate pathway has a high flux in S. stipitis, and the organism is capable of fermenting xylose. Additionally, the cluster includes various chemicals, such as yeast extract, ammonium sulfate, and YPD medium, which are used in the growth and fermentation processes of the microorganisms.",
